@*
    Idea-type badge (SPEC/20-feature-idea-type-fields.md "Type appearance"). Renders a type's color +
    icon + name as a pill, tying idea types into the same visual system as statuses and priority. Used on
    the Idea Types admin list, the idea create form preview, idea detail, and idea cards/list.

    Colors come in as inline styles (a soft tint of the type color for the fill, the color itself for the
    text) so no shared app.css class is needed and the palette follows whatever the admin picked. A null
    color falls back to a neutral badge; a null icon simply omits the glyph.

    The name is always rendered: colour may never be the only carrier of meaning (SPEC/decisions.md,
    2026-08-31), and the earlier icon-only form left the type as a coloured dot with the name only on a
    tooltip — invisible to screen readers and unreachable on touch. Set Compact for tight spots
    (swimlane/list cards), which keeps the badge small and lets a long name ellipsize; the full name
    stays on the tooltip.
*@
<span class="typebadge @(Compact ? "compact" : null)" style="@Style()" title="@Tooltip()">
    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Icon))
    {
        <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true">@Icon</span>
    }
    <span class="nm">@Name</span>
</span>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    [Parameter] public string? ColorHex { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string? Icon { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Tighter form for cards where space is short — the name stays, but may ellipsize.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Compact { get; set; }

    private string Style()
    {
        if (IsHex(ColorHex))
        {
            // #RRGGBB + "22" ≈ 13% alpha fill; the solid color is used for the text/glyph.
            return $"background:{ColorHex}22;color:{ColorHex}";
        }
        return "background:#f1f0ee;color:var(--ink-2)";
    }

    // Only the compact form can truncate, so only it needs the name repeated on hover.
    private string? Tooltip() => Compact ? Name : null;

    private static bool IsHex(string? value) =>
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(value) && value.Length == 7 && value[0] == '#';
}
